agent: route JobStarted through the recorder pending queue

The tool hook used to append JobStarted to the session cursor at hook-fire
time, mid-tool-call. The user turn that triggered the spawn had not been
flushed yet (turns only flush at round checkpoints), so JobStarted chained
off the pre-turn leaf (typically the system message). Rolling back past
the spawning turn in /tree kept the JobStarted on the new lineage, and
reconcile_jobs_after_lineage_switch saw the job as in-lineage: no kill,
no stale-notice.

Queue JobStarted into SessionRecorder::pending_job_lifecycle and drain it
in append_pending so the parent_id chains off the current turn's events.
The rollback then drops the JobStarted, and reconcile cancels the
off-lineage job.

JobFinished still writes directly: it can fire long after the spawning
turn ends, when the recorder is already dropped, so routing through the
queue would lose it.
